From 4f5b3c59f1dfff709934af4ba4c07dcb6216d150 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuk3s <44327449+nuk3s@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:09:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kv-offload): turn disk faults into misses and degrade
 the tier

Upstream base: the patch applies to local-inference-lab/vllm at
19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 after the 702 patches of
spark-ds41f-1120 (candidate-62, 0001 to 0829) and patches 9030 to 9032
of this series.

Rationale: an exception in an IO thread of the disk backend ended the
thread. The failed load and every later load on that rank were then
never reported, so each request with a disk hit waited forever while
/health stayed up, and failed stores kept their GPU blocks pinned; a
CPU-only probe on the tree of 9030 to 9032 showed both. This patch makes
every disk transfer end within a bound and keeps a fault from serving
any state:
- DiskBackend runs each queued transfer under one handler. A failed or
  short preadv or pwritev raises DiskTierError with the errno and the
  slot, and that or any other exception marks the event failed and
  records the first fault of the rank, while the IO thread stays alive.
  After the first fault, every queued transfer fails at once with no
  I/O. abandon() stops the copies of an event before its next DMA, and
  the check runs under a lock.
- SimpleCPUOffloadWorker abandons a transfer that is still pending
  disk_io_timeout_s after submission (a new kv_connector_extra_config
  key, 15 s by default), and every pending transfer of an IO thread that
  is no longer running. It drains the load stream before it releases a
  load. A failed load is reported in finished_recving and in
  failed_recving (get_transfer_results), and a failed store is reported
  complete and in failed_store_events. The worker metadata carries the
  first fault of the rank once, as (rank, op, slot, errno, message).
- SimpleCPUOffloadScheduler marks the tier degraded at the first fault
  record or failed load from any rank. From then on every lookup misses,
  no store is selected, and the queued finish-time stores are released.
  A store that failed on any rank is dropped once all ranks have
  reported it, so its slots are never published and its GPU references
  are released. The scheduler logs one error line at the change, with
  the rank, the operation, the slot, and the errno, and none afterwards.
- The scheduler side exports the stats as Prometheus series: the gauge
  vllm:kv_offload_disk_degraded and the counters
  vllm:kv_offload_disk_loads_total, _load_failures_total,
  _stored_blocks_total, _store_failed_blocks_total, and _io_errors_total.
- The connector warns when the disk backend runs with a
  kv_load_failure_policy other than "recompute", because the default
  "fail" ends the request where "recompute" computes it again.
A request that waits on a load is released as a miss at the first engine
step after the fault is caught, or, when the I/O hangs, at the first
step after disk_io_timeout_s from submission on the slowest rank. The
fork's KVOutputAggregator releases the request only when all ranks have
reported, and _handle_failed_recving (with kv_load_failure_policy
"recompute") frees the loaded blocks uncached and computes the request
again.

Quality implications: a disk fault costs one prefill of the affected
request and turns the tier off until the next engine start, and no state
from a failed transfer reaches the model.

Tests: tests/v1/simple_kv_offload/test_ds41_tier_faults.py runs a real
O_DIRECT file with host copies and injects EIO on a read and on a write,
a short read, a load thread that ends in the middle of a load, and a
read that hangs. The hung read is released at 0.3 to 0.5 s with a 0.3 s
timeout, and the late read copies nothing. Further tests check that the
fault reaches the scheduler from rank 1 of three through
KVOutputAggregator, that a store failed on one rank is dropped from the
index, and that the metric names are right. On the CPU path the offload
suite passed 139 tests, with 2 CUDA-only modules skipped. These tests
run the stream drain and the abandoned DMA of the CUDA side with host
copies only. On DGX Spark hardware the patch ran as part of the whole
series, and its fault path ran once there: when the tier file of one
rank was truncated to 0 bytes, the request was computed again and the
tier marked itself degraded.

Upstream status: the patch is proposed to spark-ds41f in
experiments/2026-11-22-kv-disk-tier and has not been submitted to
local-inference-lab/vllm.
